From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0383-mem-audit-01-stream-ring-switch.patch

Source: 0383-mem-audit-01-stream-ring-switch.patch
Core patch, on core16 (through 0181). Paths are the submodule's.

The ring is 128 MiB on the console: all 44 EDEN_REFUSED_STAGING stream lines of run62 print the
real member, and it is a dedicated allocation (VMA blocks are 16 MiB here), so a smaller ring
really goes back. 64 gives 64 MiB back, 32 gives 96.

EDEN_STREAM_RING_MIB=<16..128> in env.txt. Unset, or out of range, as before; try 64 first.
Replaces fable-trick-09 (EDEN_STREAM_BUFFER_MIB, in no stack): do not use both.

The ring keeps its 16 regions, so the fence checks and the wrap do not change, only how often
they run. The real GetStreamBuffer/WaitForStream, run against a model GPU at 128/64/32/16 MiB,
handed out no range still in flight.

What it costs: a region is 1/16 of the ring. Uploads over a region go through a staging buffer,
which can be refused, and those buffers hold memory for a while, so part of the gain can come
back. Under 16 MiB a region would be less than the 1 MiB UploadInChunks falls back to, hence the
floor. A full ring also reaches the wait that ends the command buffer in a draw's setup more often.

Async decode slices were a fixed 8 MiB, which is one region only at 128 MiB. They now stay within
a region, or they would need a staging buffer just when the pool has none and hold their decoded
data while waiting. Unset on the console a region is 8 MiB, so nothing changes.

Syntax-compiled for the PS5 target with warnings on, TextureCache instantiated for Vulkan and
OpenGL, through prepare-vulkan-port.py (same skipped anchors as before). Not built, not run on the
console.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

